Ex. No.: 02              LINKED LIST 
Date: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
Aim 
To create a singly linked list and insert a new node at a specific position 
Algorithm  
1. Start the program.  
2. Create three nodes and assign values to them.  
3. Create a new node with the value to be inserted.  
4. Link the first, second, and third nodes.  
5. Insert the new node between the second and third nodes.  
6. Display the updated linked list.  
7. Stop the program. 
Program 
#include <stdio.h> 
#include <stdlib.h> 
struct node 
{ 
      int data; 
      struct node *next; 
}; 
int main() 
{ 
    struct node *head, *second, *third, *newnode; 
    // Create first node 
    head = (struct node *)malloc(sizeof(struct node)); 
    head->data = 20; 
    // Create second node 
    second = (struct node *)malloc(sizeof(struct node)); 
    second->data = 30;  
    // Create third node 
    third = (struct node *)malloc(sizeof(struct node)); 
    third->data = 40; 
 
    // Create new node 
    newnode = (struct node *)malloc(sizeof(struct node)); 
    newnode->data = 25; 
    // Original Linked List 
    head->next = second; 
    second->next = third; 
    third->next = NULL; 
    // Insert new node at specific position 
    second->next = newnode; 
    newnode->next = third; 
    // Display Linked List 
    printf("Linked List after insertion:\n"); 
 
    while(head != NULL) 
    { 
        printf("%d -> ", head->data); 
        head = head->next; 
    } 
    printf("NULL"); 
    return 0; 
} 
Output 
Linked List after insertion: 
20 -> 30 -> 25 -> 40 -> NULL 
Result 
Thus, a singly linked list was created successfully, and a new node was inserted at the specified 
position.
